    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW25KWiJPRkGcgDQT8pc4YUMR)_\n\nFollows #354 and #358 (merged).\n\n## What\n- Author candidates can be dropped for later, with the mechanism of the other lint reports (`sp-batch-report`: `d` drop, `u` restore, `A` apply):\n  - in the lint report: `d` drops the entry at point, `u` on a dropped one brings it back, `A` runs the author fixes with what is left\n  - dropped entries move to a \"Dropped from the list\" section at the end, with their count\n  - in an author batch question (all three steps): `d` asks which entries of the batch to drop, `u` which dropped ones to bring back (comma separated, with completion); the batch is shown again each time\n  - a dropped entry is left out of all three author steps, now and in later runs; a brought-back entry is part of the next run, not of the batch on screen\n  - `M-x sp-bibtex-lint-restore-dropped` brings entries back without the report\n- Where the stash lives: the list `sp-bibtex-lint--excluded`, keys `FILE::ENTRY-KEY`. It lasts for the Emacs session, like the dropped entries of the other lint reports, and is not saved to disk. Nothing in the `.bib` file or the notes changes.\n- Field order and indentation ignore drops (they are whole-file fixes). The report's counts for those two buttons include dropped entries.\n- Literate doc updated as bullet lists; it tangles to the committed `sp-bibprocess.el`.\n\n## Tests\n- 49 tests (this file and `sp-batch-report`) pass in Emacs 29 with `sp-cache-dir` and `sp-var-dir` defined. New: drop in an author batch, dropped stays out of later runs, restore with `u`, dropping the whole batch writes nothing, order ignores drops, drop in a notes batch, `d`/`u` in the report, restore command.\n- Not run on the real `.bib` files or in Emacs 31.\n\nNo CHANGELOG edits, per the nightly-tidy rule. The branch is not prefixed with the PR number, because the session's branch name was fixed.\n\n---\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiCsguMS2m92TG5VLGt)_",
